      en: "Saadian Tombs is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Morocco. A historic cemetery in Marrakech housing the tombs of the Saadian sultans from the late 16th century. The site was only rediscovered in 1917. Hidden for over 300 years. Famous for the Hall of 12 Columns. This site holds particular significance in the history of Morocco. Like many notable places in Morocco, it combines regional character with wider significance. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Morocco."
